## Changing String Case

`str_upper` converts to uppercase, `str_lower` converts to lowercase. Essential for case-insensitive comparisons.

### str_upper — Uppercase

```xiom
let name = "alice";
let upper = str_upper(name);  // "ALICE"

let mixed = "Hello World";
let shout = str_upper(mixed);  // "HELLO WORLD"
```

### str_lower — Lowercase

```xiom
let name = "ALICE";
let lower = str_lower(name);  // "alice"

let mixed = "Hello World";
let whisper = str_lower(mixed);  // "hello world"
```

### Case-Insensitive Comparison

```xiom
fn eq_ignore_case(a: Str, b: Str) -> Bool {
  return str_lower(a) == str_lower(b);
}

let same = eq_ignore_case("Hello", "HELLO");   // true
let diff = eq_ignore_case("Hello", "World");   // false
```

### Practical Uses

```xiom
// Normalize user input
fn normalize_username(name: Str) -> Str {
  return str_trim(str_lower(name));
}

// Check answer (case insensitive)
fn check_answer(user_answer: Str, correct: Str) -> Bool {
  return str_lower(user_answer) == str_lower(correct);
}

// Title case (first letter uppercase)
fn title_case(s: Str) -> Str {
  if s.len() == 0 { return s; }
  let first = str_upper(str_slice(s, 0, 1));
  let rest = str_slice(s, 1, s.len());
  return first + str_lower(rest);
}
```

### Chaining with Other Operations

```xiom
fn clean_and_match(input: Str, expected: Str) -> Bool {
  let cleaned = str_trim(input);
  let normalized = str_lower(cleaned);
  return normalized == str_lower(expected);
}
```

